<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sitobu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sitobu is remembered in Dagomba tradition as a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/na-gbewaa">Na Gbewaa</a>, founder of the Mamprugu kingdom, and as the ancestor of the royal house of Dagbon in present-day northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana">Ghana</a>. After a dispute among Na Gbewaa's sons over the succession he moved west with his followers. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/na-nyagse">Na Nyagse</a> completed the conquests that created the kingdom.</p></div>
